course: dictionary
lesson: 853
title: Better: more good, less ill, or should
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Better is a small word with several jobs. Most often it compares two things and says one is more good than the other. «A score of 9 is better than a score of 7» means 9 is the more good score. Look for the word than, because it often tells you a comparison is coming.
explain: Better can also describe how someone does something. «She sings better now» means she sings in a more good way than before. Better can also mean less ill: «I feel better today» means you are not as poorly as you were.
explain: Watch for «had better», which means should. «You had better hurry» does not mean you are good at hurrying; it means you should hurry. Read the words around better and ask which meaning fits.
fact: Better is the comparison form of good: good, better, best.
fact: Better is also the comparison form of well: well, better, best.
fact: «Better buy» in shopping maths compares the price of one item, so you can work out which deal is cheaper.
fact: «Had better» means should, as in «you had better hurry».
fact: «Your betters» is an old-fashioned noun meaning people thought to be higher in rank, and today we do not sort people into betters and lesser folk.
exercise: In «A score of 9 is better than a score of 7», which score is the better one? | *9 | 7 | Neither one | They are the same
exercise: «I feel better today.» What does better mean here? | Faster | *Less ill | Louder | More clever
exercise: «You had better hurry.» What does had better mean? | *Should | Has already hurried | Was faster than | Is not allowed to
test: In «She sings better now», what does better tell us? | When she sings | Who she sings to | *How she sings, in a more good way | Where she sings
test: Which word is the comparison form of well? | bested | good | wells | *better
exam: Which sentence uses better to mean should? | *You had better leave now | I feel better today | He sings better than me | Her score is better than mine
